---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {workouts} from '../data/workouts';
const photos=['photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a','photo-1517836357463-d25dfeac3438','photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a','photo-1581009146145-b5ef050c2e1e'];
const faqs = [
  { question: 'How do I work out at home?', answer: 'Choose a routine that matches your current experience and available time. Clear a safe space, begin with a short warm-up, follow a few strength or cardio exercises with good control, and finish with an easy cool-down. Rest when needed and build your routine gradually.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my back at home?', answer: 'Try controlled bodyweight movements such as bird dogs and superman raises, which train the back and trunk without equipment. For a pulling movement, use a securely packed, manageable backpack for bent-over rows. Keep your back comfortable and stop if you feel pain.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my legs at home?', answer: 'Build a leg session around bodyweight squats, reverse lunges, glute bridges, calf raises, and wall sits. Start with a small number of sets, use a chair or wall for balance if helpful, and choose a range of motion you can control.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out at home without equipment?', answer: 'Use bodyweight exercises such as squats, wall or incline push-ups, lunges, glute bridges, planks, and marching in place. Arrange a few movements into a short circuit with rest between rounds. A stable chair can be optional support, but avoid unstable furniture.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my chest at home?', answer: 'Push-up variations train the chest along with other upper-body muscles. Begin with wall or incline push-ups if floor push-ups are too challenging, then progress to standard push-ups when you can keep a steady, straight body position. Move with control and rest between sets.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my triceps at home?', answer: 'Close-grip push-ups and diamond push-ups emphasize the triceps while also involving the chest and shoulders. Choose a hand position that feels comfortable and use an incline or knee-supported variation to reduce difficulty. Chair dips can bother some shoulders, so skip them if they cause discomfort.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my lats at home?', answer: 'At-home lat training can be limited without a safe pulling setup. A bent-over row using a securely closed backpack with a light, manageable load is one option. Keep your back neutral, pull the bag toward your torso, and lower it slowly. Do not use a door, table, or other support unless it is designed to hold your weight safely.' },
  { question: 'How do I motivate myself to work out at home?', answer: 'Make the first step small: choose a short routine, schedule a realistic time, and set out the space or clothes beforehand. Track completed sessions to notice consistency, and select activities you do not mind repeating. If you miss a day, simply return to the routine when you are ready.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my shoulders at home?', answer: 'Arm circles and plank shoulder taps are accessible options, while pike push-ups are more demanding. Start with movements that match your current strength, keep your shoulders comfortable, and move slowly enough to maintain control. Use a wall for balance only when the setup is stable.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my lower back at home?', answer: 'Bird dogs and gentle, controlled superman raises can train the muscles around the trunk and back. Focus on a neutral spine and small, controlled movements rather than lifting as high as possible. Stop if an exercise causes pain, and seek qualified advice for persistent back symptoms.' },
  { question: 'How do I work out my upper chest at home?', answer: 'Incline push-ups are often easier to scale and train the chest, shoulders, and arms; a decline push-up shifts the body angle but is more challenging and is not suitable for every beginner. Prioritize comfortable shoulder motion and solid form instead of choosing an advanced variation before you are ready.' },
  { question: 'How do I maximize my home workout routine?', answer: 'Choose a clear goal, use a routine you can repeat, and prioritize controlled technique, suitable effort, rest, and recovery. Increase repetitions or difficulty gradually when your current routine feels manageable. Consistent sessions, enough sleep, and balanced everyday eating support a sustainable approach.' },
];
const faqStructuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title="Home Workout Plans and Exercises for Beginners" description="Find beginner-friendly home workout plans, no-equipment exercises, and simple routines to help you move consistently at home." active="/"><section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Your fitness journey starts here</span><h1>Home Workout Plans to Build a <span>Stronger You.</span></h1><p class="hero-copy">You don't need an expensive gym membership or fancy equipment to become healthier. Start with simple workouts, build consistency, and improve one day at a time.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="/workouts/">Start your journey <span>&#8599;</span></a><a class="btn btn-light" href="/workouts/">Explore workouts</a></div></div><div class="hero-visual"><img class="hero-photo" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85" alt="Person stretching in a bright, comfortable home" fetchpriority="high"/><div class="float-card float-a"><span class="dot"></span>Beginner friendly<small>Start where you are</small></div><div class="float-card float-b">No equipment needed<small>Just a little space</small></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-white"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">A simpler way to move</span><h2>Fitness should be simple.</h2></div><p>Easy Home Workout makes it easier to understand exercise and get moving in a way that fits your life. No pressure to be perfect&middot;just practical support for your next step.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="card feature-card"><div class="icon">&middot;</div><h3>No gym required</h3><p>Build a routine in your living room with bodyweight movements and everyday space.</p></article><article class="card feature-card"><div class="icon">&#8599;</div><h3>Beginner friendly</h3><p>Clear instructions and approachable options help you begin with confidence.</p></article><article class="card feature-card"><div class="icon">&#8599;</div><h3>Your own pace</h3><p>Choose a level that feels right and make steady progress without comparison.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="fitness-goals"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Find your direction</span><h2>What would you like to work on?</h2></div></div><div class="grid-4">{[['Build muscle','Strength you can build over time','photo-1583454110551-21f2fa2afe61','/goals/build-muscle/'],['Lose weight','Support healthy habits and movement','photo-1517836357463-d25dfeac3438','/goals/weight-management/'],['General fitness','Feel more capable day to day','photo-1571019613454-1cb2f99b2d8b','/goals/general-fitness/'],['Flexibility','Move comfortably through your day','photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a','/goals/flexibility/']].map(([title,desc,img,href])=><a class="goal-card" href={href}><img loading="lazy" src={`https://images.unsplash.com/${img}?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=80`} alt={`${title} home fitness activity`}/><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{desc}</p></div></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section section-white"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Move today</span><h2>Popular workouts</h2></div><a class="card-link" href="/workouts/">View all workouts &#8599;</a></div><div class="grid-3">{workouts.slice(0,3).map((w,i)=><article class="card workout-card"><img loading="lazy" src={`https://images.unsplash.com/${w.image}?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=80`} alt={`${w.title} at home`}/><div class="card-pad"><span class="pill">{w.level}</span><h3 style="margin-top:12px">{w.title}</h3><div class="meta"><span>&#9711; {w.duration}</span><span>&#9711; {w.equipment}</span></div><p>{w.desc}</p><a class="card-link" href={`/workouts/${w.slug}/`}>View workout &#8599;</a></div></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap center"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">A few simple steps</span><h2>How Easy Home Workout works</h2><p>Start with what matters to you, then keep it manageable.</p></div><div class="steps"><div><div class="step-num">01</div><h3>Choose your goal</h3><p>Find a direction that feels meaningful to you today.</p></div><div><div class="step-num">02</div><h3>Follow your workout</h3><p>Use clear movement guidance and adjust as needed.</p></div><div><div class="step-num">03</div><h3>Track your progress</h3><p>Celebrate the sessions you complete on your own device.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="banner"><div><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#d7f36b">A gentle place to begin</span><h2>30 days, one small step at a time.</h2><p>A flexible beginner challenge blends short workouts, mobility, and recovery days. Complete it at your own pace and save progress in this browser.</p><a class="btn btn-lime" href="/challenge/">Start the challenge &#8599;</a></div><div><strong>Week 1</strong><p>Build the habit</p><strong>Week 2</strong><p>Develop consistency</p><strong>Weeks 3 and 4</strong><p>Strength & confidence</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-white"><div class="wrap split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Fuel for everyday life</span><h2>Nutrition without the noise.</h2><p>Learn the basics of balanced meals, hydration, and affordable foods. No crash diets or complicated rules&middot;just useful information to help you make choices that work for you.</p><a class="btn btn-light" href="/nutrition/">Read the nutrition guide &#8599;</a></div><img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1490645935967-10de6ba17061?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85" alt="Colorful balanced meal with vegetables and grains"/></div></section>
<section class="section section-white"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">A practical guide to moving at home</span><h2>A home workout system that meets you where you are.</h2></div></div><div style="max-width:820px"><h3>Start with a home workout that feels manageable</h3><p>Getting more active does not have to begin with a complicated schedule or a room full of equipment. Easy Home Workout is a simple home fitness resource for people who want clear instructions, realistic routines, and a comfortable place to begin. Explore a home workout by duration, difficulty, and focus, then choose the session that fits your day. You can exercise in a living room, bedroom, or any clear space where you can move safely.</p><h3>Build strength with home workout exercises</h3><p>The exercise library explains how to set up and perform familiar home workout exercises, including squats, push-ups, lunges, planks, and mobility movements. Each guide describes the starting position, the movement steps, suggested sets or timing, and common form mistakes. Easier variations can help you adapt movements to your current ability. Take breaks when you need them, move in a controlled way, and choose a comfortable range of motion. Clear guidance can make it easier to understand what a routine asks you to do before you start.</p><h3>Choose a home workout without equipment</h3><p>A home workout without equipment can use bodyweight movements and a small amount of floor space. The plans identify when no equipment is needed and when an everyday stable support or optional backpack is suggested. If you are looking for a home workout no equipment routine, begin with a short beginner session or a low-impact cardio option. You can also browse individual exercises and combine simple movements into a home workout plan that suits your schedule. Start with a pace you can maintain; you do not need to copy an advanced routine to make a useful start.</p><h3>Find an at home workout plan for your level</h3><p>Not sure where to begin? A beginner home workout plan no equipment can help remove the guesswork by setting out a warm-up, a manageable group of exercises, rest periods, and a cool-down. As you gain experience, explore intermediate strength sessions and more challenging full-body routines. The workout pages show duration, difficulty, focus, and equipment notes so you can make an informed choice. Use the plans as flexible guidance rather than a test: shorten a session, rest longer, or choose an easier variation when that feels appropriate.</p><h3>Make home workout routines part of everyday life</h3><p>Consistency is easier when the routine fits real life. Choose a day and time that generally works, keep your first sessions brief, and allow recovery between harder efforts. Easy Home Workout also offers a 30-day beginner challenge with a mix of movement, mobility, and rest days. Mark completed activities on your device and return to your progress page to review your saved workout history. This home workout system keeps tracking in your browser, so no account is required. Progress can mean showing up, learning a movement, or finding a routine you enjoy; it does not need to mean doing more every session.</p><h3>Support your workouts with useful fitness education</h3><p>Exercise is one part of looking after yourself. Read the nutrition guide for approachable information about balanced meals, hydration, and everyday food choices. Use the fitness tools for general estimates and simple tracking, remembering that calculators are not medical assessments or personal prescriptions. Needs differ between individuals, and professional guidance may be useful when you have health concerns or specific goals. Easy Home Workout is designed to make home fitness easier to explore, with practical information for beginners and adaptable ideas for people who already exercise. Choose your goal, find a suitable workout, and take one steady step at a time.</p><p>Ready to begin? <a href="/workouts/">Explore the home workout plans</a>, learn a movement in the <a href="/exercises/">exercise library</a>, or start the <a href="/challenge/">30-day home fitness challenge</a>.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="home-workout-faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Answers for getting started</span><h2 id="home-workout-faq">Home workout FAQs</h2></div><p>Practical answers to common questions about building strength and getting active at home.</p></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => <details class="faq-item"><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap center"><span class="eyebrow">Your next step</span><h2>Your first step is the most important one.</h2><p>Choose one small way to move today. You can build from there.</p><a class="btn" href="/workouts/">Start your fitness journey &#8599;</a></div></section>
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqStructuredData)} />
</Layout>
<style>
  .faq-list { display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 900px; }
  .faq-item { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 19px 22px; }
  .faq-item summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; list-style: none; position: relative; padding-right: 28px; }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item summary::after { content: '+'; position: absolute; right: 0; color: var(--green); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1; }
  .faq-item[open] summary::after { content: '−'; }
  .faq-item p { margin: 13px 0 0; }
</style>

